# <%= name %>

A Roblox game built with [KRF](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/) `<%= runtime.package %>@<%= runtime.version %>`.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

<% if (options.places) { -%>
`npm run dev` builds the start place, opens it in Roblox Studio and serves it with Rojo. Connect the Rojo plugin, then press Play. Saving captures that place into `world/<place>/` and `places/<place>.project.json`. All places share `src/`. Commit `wally.lock`.

Run `npm run dev -- --place <name>` to work on another place or `npm run build` to build every place without opening Studio. `krf.startPlace` in `package.json` selects the start place for setup, typechecking and Studio tests. Run `npm run sourcemap` to refresh VS Code's map after changing the start place.
<% } else { -%>
`npm run dev` opens `<%= name %>.rbxl` in Roblox Studio and serves the project with Rojo. Connect the Rojo plugin, then press Play. Commit `wally.lock`.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.mode === "full") { -%>

<% if (!options.places) { -%>
While `npm run dev` runs, saving in Studio captures your world into `world/` and `default.project.json`. Review and commit those changes like code. See [World](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/world).

For a [game with named places](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/cloud-deployment#deploy-an-experience-with-multiple-places), `npm run dev` opens the start place. Use `npm run dev -- --place <name>` to work on another place.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>

This is a Hybrid project: Rojo syncs `src` and `Packages`, and `<%= name %>.rbxl` owns the world. Save your world in it; `npm run dev` creates it once and never rebuilds it. To keep part of the world in Git, [opt a folder in](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/world#hybrid-projects).
<% } -%>
<% if (options.agents) { -%>

`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the KRF skill tell coding agents how to build this game with KRF. The skill is in `.agents/skills/krf/` for Codex and `.claude/skills/krf/` for Claude Code; keep both copies the same.
<% } -%>

## Cloud deployment

Use [the cloud guide](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/cloud-deployment) to set up an assigned group Dev place or QA and Production releases for a Full project. Local build and Studio Play work without cloud setup.

## Scripts

| Script | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Builds and opens the place in Studio, serves it with Rojo and captures Studio saves; `-- --no-open` only serves, `-- --no-syncback` skips them |
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>
| `npm run build` | Builds `build/<%= name %>.rbxl` from the starter world, without touching your place |
<% } else if (options.places) { -%>
| `npm run build` | Builds every named place and prints the paths to the resulting binaries |
<% } else { -%>
| `npm run build` | Builds `<%= name %>.rbxl` |
<% } -%>
| `npm test` | Runs the Jest specs in `tests` inside Roblox Studio |
| `npm run test:studio` | Plays the game in Studio with a server and two clients and checks that KRF starts |
| `npm run world:syncback` | Syncs a saved place back into source once. Use `-- --input <file>` for a different Studio file<% if (options.places) { %>, or `-- --place <name>` for a named place other than the start place<% } %>. See [World](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/world). |
| `npm run format` | Formats `src` and `tests` |
| `npm run check` | Checks formatting, lints and type checks without changing files |
| `npm run createAction`, `createTag`, `createResource`, `createProperty`, `createController`, `createCommand`, `createHint`, `createDomain`, `createPresentation` | Creates a definition. See [Generate a definition](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/reference/getting-started/project-tools#generate-a-definition). |
